This is my pet "true rumour that should be false".  Elven armour can
safely be enchanted when it is at +5 or less (and so can cornuthaums
if you are a wizard), which means that it can safely be got to +7 by
disenchanting it if it reaches +6.  Polypiling enough +7 elven armour
will eventually give you +7 gauntlets of dexterity and a +7 helm of
brilliance.

As you'll note, that will get Dex, Int and Wis to 25, which is one
reason why I don't like that rumour.  The other reason is that I'd
take rings of gain constitution over rings of adornment.
